Hi Jesse,

If this is the first time you've done spatial R stuff, I highly recommend this resource as a place to get started and be reminded of how to do some useful things   http://www.rspatial.org/ and the raster <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/raster/raster.pdf> package in general.  These resources will help you get your data (shapefile?)  into a R working environment.

Based on the landscape metrics link you shared, it looks like you'll need some even more specialized R package to do your calculations, unless you want to write your own functions.  Looks like SDMTools <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/SDMTools/SDMTools.pdf> may have some of what you need, specifically the function PatchStat <https://www.rforge.net/doc/packages/SDMTools/PatchStat.html> ???

Scott

